      "id": "r2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "must confess, somewhat difficult to understand, what motive",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "there can have been in giving to the work the name of a person,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "who does not appear to have been ever in occupation of a throne,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "except from the very tradition which is here to be distrusted.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "Nor is it quite in keeping with all ideas of propriety, that an",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "utter stranger should venture to touch on such a delicate topic",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "as that alluded to in the second couplet above spoken of.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/faded along the gutter"
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Another theory which has been suggested with regard to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the composition of these S′atakas is that they were mere compi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "lations made by Bhartṛihari, a mere collection of “elegant",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "extracts” from the works of previous writers. This theory seems",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "to be in part countenanced by Bohlen who adduces the parallel",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "example of the sayings ascribed to Solomon and others.[*] That",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "this again is possible I do not deny. For besides the parallel",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "examples alluded to by Bohlen, there is also to be considered",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "in favour of this theory the circumstance that the Hindus have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "always been fond of these Subhâshitas with which their con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "versation in ordinary life is to this day considerably interlard-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "ed.[†] In further support of the theory it is to be observed that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "some of the Stanzas occurring in these S′atakas are also to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "found in other works still extant.[‡] Against the reception of",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/faded along the gutter"
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "days gone by went through a somewhat extensive course of instruction",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "in which poetry was not by any means neglected. Surely then it is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "also possible, to say the least of it, that an individual prince might turn",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "to be even a very good poet.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/faded along the gutter"
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "* See Bohlen Præfatio p. vi.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "† For a few more observations on this point see the tractate entitled",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "“ Was the Râmâyana copied from Homer ? ” p. 58.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/faded along the gutter"
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "‡ A further support to the theory may be found in the circumstance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "that most of the MSS. of the S′atakas differ from each other as to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "number and even the position of the Stanzas. In the sequel we",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
